<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	20261002 gjw CarPlay.

	com.apple.developer.carplay-audio is a REQUEST-ONLY entitlement. Apple
	assigned it to the account on 20261002; before that it could not be used
	at all. Having it on the account is not enough on its own:

	  1. Tick CarPlay Audio App on the com.togaware.radiopod App ID.
	  2. REGENERATE the "RadioPod App Store" provisioning profile. A profile
	     is a snapshot and does not pick up a new capability by itself. Miss
	     this and signing fails with "Provisioning profile ... doesn't
	     include the com.apple.developer.carplay-audio entitlement", which
	     reads as though the entitlement is missing rather than the profile
	     being stale.
	  3. Update the IOS_PROVISION_PROFILE secret from the new profile,
	     base64 -w0 as in ignore/IOS.md step 6.

	ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj points CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS at
	this file in all three configurations. The file itself was missing from
	the repository until now: .gitignore excludes ios/Runner/ wholesale, so
	the CarPlay pull request's new files were dropped silently while the
	project changes referencing them went through. It is force-added.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.carplay-audio</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
